Gimble Whizzspark, a gnome warlock with a top hat askew and a pocket full of sparkles, tromped through Stranglethorn’s jungles, his succubus Lilithia trailing behind—all curves and crimson, her tail flicking like a smoldering whip. “Really, Gimble,” she purred, “you couldn’t pick a *less* mosquito-infested quest? ‘Collect 10 jaguar pelts’? Adorable.”  

A raptora roared, lunging. Lilithia giggled, snapping her fingers. The beast froze, eyes glazed—seduced. “See?” she said, but before Gimble could cheer, a pirate with a parrot squawked from a tree, shooting an arrow. The raptora, aggro spiked, snapped free and charged Gimble. He yelped, summoning a firebolt that barely missed his own foot. Lilithia sighed, slashing the raptor apart. “Next time, *aim* the charm, love.” Gimble panted, grinning. “Worth it. You look *devastating* when you’re mad.”  


**Answer:**  
Succubi’s Seduce skill, while powerful for crowd control, is risky—if interrupted or aggro shifts, seduced mobs may turn on the warlock. Voidwalkers, with their reliable Shield of the Damned and tanky nature, felt safer for casual leveling, making them more commonly seen despite succubi’s better raw stats. [end of text]


